DIGITAL SIGNATURE TOOL
======================

A simple JPEG digital signature tool using:

    RSA-2048
    RSA-PSS
    SHA-256

The tool creates a separate signed copy of the original JPEG.

The original image is never modified.

------------------------------------------------------------
PROJECT STRUCTURE
------------------------------------------------------------

.
├── dsign.py
├── org
│   └── jrsu.jpeg
├── private_key.pem
├── public_key.pem
└── readme


------------------------------------------------------------
REQUIREMENTS
------------------------------------------------------------

Python 3

Python package:

    cryptography


Install cryptography:

    python3 -m pip install cryptography

If using a Python virtual environment:

    source /opt/python-venv/bin/activate

    python3 -m pip install cryptography


------------------------------------------------------------
1. GENERATE RSA PRIVATE KEY
------------------------------------------------------------

Generate a 2048-bit RSA private key:

    openssl genrsa -out private_key.pem 2048


This creates:

    private_key.pem


The private key is used to create the digital signature.

Keep the private key secure.


------------------------------------------------------------
2. GENERATE RSA PUBLIC KEY
------------------------------------------------------------

Generate the public key from the private key:

    openssl rsa -in private_key.pem -pubout -out public_key.pem


This creates:

    public_key.pem


The public key is used to verify the digital signature.


------------------------------------------------------------
3. CHECK PROJECT FILES
------------------------------------------------------------

Run:

    tree


Expected structure:

    .
    ├── dsign.py
    ├── org
    │   └── jrsu.jpeg
    ├── private_key.pem
    ├── public_key.pem
    └── readme


------------------------------------------------------------
4. VIEW HELP
------------------------------------------------------------

Run:

    python3 dsign.py --help


Available commands:

    sign
    check
    verify


------------------------------------------------------------
5. SIGN THE IMAGE
------------------------------------------------------------

The original image is:

    ./org/jrsu.jpeg


Run:

    python3 dsign.py sign -privatekey ./private_key.pem -file ./org/jrsu.jpeg


The program creates:

    ./org/jrsu_signed.jpeg


The original file:

    ./org/jrsu.jpeg


is not modified.


The signature is embedded inside the signed JPEG.

No separate .sig file is created.


Expected output:

    ✓ SIGNED
    Original   : /home/bsilent/Downloads/org/jrsu.jpeg
    Signed     : /home/bsilent/Downloads/org/jrsu_signed.jpeg
    SHA-256    : <SHA-256 HASH>
    Algorithm  : RSA-2048 + PSS + SHA-256
    Signed At  : <DATE AND TIME>


------------------------------------------------------------
6. VERIFY THE SIGNED IMAGE
------------------------------------------------------------

Verify the signed image using the public key:

    python3 dsign.py check -publickey ./public_key.pem -file ./org/jrsu_signed.jpeg


If the signature matches:

    ✓ SIGNATURE VALID
    --------------------------------
    File      : /home/bsilent/Downloads/org/jrsu_signed.jpeg
    SHA-256   : <SHA-256 HASH>
    Algorithm : RSA-2048 + PSS + SHA-256
    --------------------------------


If the image or signature has been modified:

    ✗ SIGNATURE INVALID
    --------------------------------
    File      : /home/bsilent/Downloads/org/jrsu_signed.jpeg
    SHA-256   : <SHA-256 HASH>
    Algorithm : RSA-2048 + PSS + SHA-256
    --------------------------------


------------------------------------------------------------
7. VERIFY COMMAND
------------------------------------------------------------

The tool also provides a verify command.

Run:

    python3 dsign.py verify -publickey ./public_key.pem -file ./org/jrsu_signed.jpeg


A valid signature produces:

    ✓ SIGNATURE VALID


An invalid signature produces:

    ✗ SIGNATURE INVALID


------------------------------------------------------------
8. COMPLETE SETUP AND RUN
------------------------------------------------------------

The complete process can be performed using these commands:

    openssl genrsa -out private_key.pem 2048

    openssl rsa -in private_key.pem -pubout -out public_key.pem

    python3 -m pip install cryptography

    python3 dsign.py sign -privatekey ./private_key.pem -file ./org/jrsu.jpeg

    python3 dsign.py check -publickey ./public_key.pem -file ./org/jrsu_signed.jpeg


------------------------------------------------------------
9. COMPLETE COMMAND FLOW
------------------------------------------------------------

Generate private key:

    openssl genrsa -out private_key.pem 2048

Generate public key:

    openssl rsa -in private_key.pem -pubout -out public_key.pem

Sign:

    python3 dsign.py sign -privatekey ./private_key.pem -file ./org/jrsu.jpeg

Check:

    python3 dsign.py check -publickey ./public_key.pem -file ./org/jrsu_signed.jpeg


------------------------------------------------------------
10. HOW IT WORKS
------------------------------------------------------------

SIGNING:

    jrsu.jpeg
        |
        v
    SHA-256
        |
        v
    RSA-PSS
        |
        v
    Private Key
        |
        v
    Digital Signature
        |
        v
    jrsu_signed.jpeg


VERIFICATION:

    jrsu_signed.jpeg
        |
        v
    Extract Embedded Signature
        |
        v
    SHA-256
        |
        v
    RSA-PSS Verification
        |
        v
    Public Key
        |
        v
    VALID / INVALID


------------------------------------------------------------
11. FILES CREATED
------------------------------------------------------------

Original image:

    org/jrsu.jpeg


Signed image:

    org/jrsu_signed.jpeg


Private key:

    private_key.pem


Public key:

    public_key.pem


No separate signature file is required.


------------------------------------------------------------
12. IMPORTANT
------------------------------------------------------------

The private key must be kept secure.

Do not share:

    private_key.pem


The public key can be shared for signature verification:

    public_key.pem


The original image remains unchanged.

The signed image is created as a separate file:

    jrsu_signed.jpeg


------------------------------------------------------------
13. ALGORITHM
------------------------------------------------------------

Key:

    RSA-2048

Signature padding:

    RSA-PSS

Hash:

    SHA-256


------------------------------------------------------------
14. QUICK COMMANDS
------------------------------------------------------------

Generate keys:

    openssl genrsa -out private_key.pem 2048

    openssl rsa -in private_key.pem -pubout -out public_key.pem


Sign:

    python3 dsign.py sign -privatekey ./private_key.pem -file ./org/jrsu.jpeg


Check:

    python3 dsign.py check -publickey ./public_key.pem -file ./org/jrsu_signed.jpeg


Verify:

    python3 dsign.py verify -publickey ./public_key.pem -file ./org/jrsu_signed.jpeg


------------------------------------------------------------
END
